class.description:
Returned by [method HEGoAssetNode.get_surface_output], and the surface counterpart of [HEGoGeoOutput]: where that one selects points, this selects primitives and turns a group of them into a Godot surface array.
[codeblock]
var output = await _await_task(asset_node.get_surface_output(["N", "uv"], ["hego_mesh_instance", "hego_material"]))

var by_instance = output.split_by("hego_mesh_instance")
for instance_name in by_instance:
    var by_material = by_instance[instance_name].split_by("hego_material")
    for material in by_material:
        var surface = by_material[material].get_surface(["hego_lod"])
        arr_mesh.add_surface_from_arrays(Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES, surface["surface_array"])
[/codeblock]

The primitive and vertex lists and the point attributes are read once for the whole mesh part. Splitting is index work; a group only compacts the points its own primitives use, and only when [method HEGoGeoPrimSelection.get_surface] is called, so a mesh split into many materials does not pay for the whole mesh per material.

Attribute values come from the same per-cook cache as every other output, so the point attributes this reads cost nothing if another output already read them.

Note that the geometry attributes HEGo reads - [code]N[/code], [code]Cd[/code], [code]uv[/code], [code]uv2[/code] and the tangents - are [b]point[/b] attributes. Promote vertex attributes to points in your HDA before outputting.
